```
<<.RepoName>>/
├── common/                        # cross-project shared plumbing
│   ├── values-dev.yaml            # env-level values shared by ALL projects (an -f overlay point)
│   ├── values-prod.yaml
│   ├── skills/<skill>/SKILL.md    # RUNTIME skills, synced into the platform
│   └── README.md                  # what the overlay points are
│                                  # (rendering is `asgard-cli render <project> <env>`, not a file here)
├── projects/<project>/
│   ├── deploy.yaml                # which envs this project deploys to + namespace + values per env
│   └── chart/
│       ├── app/templates/<kind>/  # one directory per CR kind, one file per CR
│       ├── values-dev.yaml        # per-project per-env (platformMainEnvironmentId, DB host …)
│       └── values-prod.yaml
├── scripts/                       # what needs a cluster or a database — the rest is asgard-cli
│   ├── check_crd_fidelity.py      # fields the CRDs would silently prune (needs kubectl)
│   └── db/                        # query + introspection helpers (add as databases are wired up)
├── .agents/skills/                # DESIGN-TIME skills — for the coding agent working in this repo
│   ├── spec-workflow/             #   turn unclear work into a reviewable spec
│   ├── semantic-layer-modeling/   #   connect to the real DBs, introspect, model a SemanticLayer
│   ├── proposal-deck/             #   a slide deck for the CUSTOMER, from their own material
│   └── asgard-cr-verification/    #   the four-step acceptance gate
├── docs/                          # Spec-Driven Development — the spec & decision layers
│   ├── README.md                  #   the index + the four-layer model + the AGENTS.md boundary
│   ├── spec-driven-development.md #   the SDD rules (status flow, task spec format, gates)
│   ├── spec/<<.SpecSlug>>/          # ★ LIVING SPEC — what the system does NOW (read this first)
│   ├── decisions/                 #   dated, immutable decision records — why it was decided
